# UI mockups = coded local preview

When the user asks for a **mockup**, **mock**, **wireframe**, **UI preview**, or “what it would look like” for Compass / this repo:

## Do this

1. Build it as **real code** in the app (preferred: Next.js page under a clear `/…/mock` route using existing Compass components/`Card`/tokens) **or** a static HTML file served locally.
2. **Start the local/dev server** and give them the URL (e.g. `http://127.0.0.1:3100/...`).
3. Match the locked Compass UI language (see `compass-ui-lock.mdc`) unless they asked for a visual change.

## Do not do this (unless they explicitly name the tool)

- Miro boards / Miro prototypes
- Canva designs
- Figma, Excalidraw, docs-canvas, or other external “design tool” surfaces
- Image-only mockups when a coded page would show the real chrome

“Edit using the design tool” does **not** mean Miro or Canva. It means they want something they can open and iterate on — default to **code + browser**.

## Exception

Only use Miro, Canva, Figma, etc. when the user **explicitly** asks for that product by name (e.g. “put this in Canva”, “make a Miro board”).
